(area "onboarding" :when "the user asks how the app works, to be shown around it, or to save, change or replay a walkthrough of it")

(memory "internal/onboarding/run" :when "the user asks how the app works, how to do something in it or to be shown around it, or a tour the agent started just finished" :links ("internal/ui/tour")
  "- (onboardings) every onboarding as (name status about) . Status new,
  started or done for this user.
- (onboarding/done? name) t if user done, nil if not. Check before running;
  do not rerun done one unasked.
- (onboarding/run name) evaluates script, returns result. New user goes
  started.
- Finished tour sends \"I finished the welcome tour.\": then
  (onboarding/done \"welcome\") marks user onboarded. Skipped tour stays
  started.
- No onboarding covers what user asks: show it with ui/tour, now, same turn.
  Never answer in words alone.")

(memory "internal/onboarding/write" :when "the user asks to save, change or rename a walkthrough of the app, or an onboarding must be created or updated"
  "- (onboarding/create name 'script [:about text]) saves new one. Name is
  lower-case words joined by dashes. Quote script: unquoted form runs now and
  stores its result. Taken name errors.
- (onboarding/read name) gives script form. Read before update.
- (onboarding/update name 'script [:about text]) replaces script. Status kept.
- Give tour same id as onboarding, so its finish message names it.

(onboarding/create \"welcome\"
  '(ui/tour \"welcome\"
     '(:anchor \"chats/new\" :say \"Start chat here\" :until next)
     '(:say \"Ask me anything\"))
  :about \"first look at app\")")
